# AI Theme addon (libs/al-web-components/.storybook/ai-theme)
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in to enable AI-derived themes during
# `pnpm --filter @southleft/al-web-components start`. The key is read by the Vite dev
# middleware in the Node process only — it is never exposed to the browser.
#
# Without it the endpoint returns 503 and the panel silently falls back to its
# local deterministic seed engine, which still produces a complete, WCAG-AA
# theme. The feature degrades; it does not break.
#
# In production the same two variables are set in the Cloudflare Pages project
# (Settings -> Environment variables), where they are read by functions/api/theme.js.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to claude-haiku-4-5 — deriving an art direction is a
# classification-shaped task with a strict output schema, so it does not need a
# larger model.
#
# If you override this, read the max_tokens comment in functions/api/theme.js:
# models newer than the 4.6 family think by default, thinking counts against
# max_tokens, and the endpoint's 800-token budget will truncate every response
# (surfacing as a 502) unless you raise it too.
# THEME_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# Figma Console MCP (agent-mediated token sync — see .altitude/FIGMA-SYNC.md)
#
# Personal Access Token with scopes: File content, File versions, Variables,
# Comments. Read by the `figma-console` entry in .mcp.json (shell env, not this
# file — export it in your shell profile or set it before launching Claude Code).
# Write operations additionally need the Desktop Bridge plugin running in Figma.
# FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN=
